      "title": "Choose EXL3 GEMM tiles that cover the output width",
      "claims": [
        {
          "text": "For A[M,K] × B[K,N], M is the row count, K the reduction dimension, and N the output width. Shapes 1–4 all use 16-row tiles; their (K,N) tiles are (16,128), (32,128), (32,256), and (16,512), with 256, 512, 512, and 256 threads respectively. Both kernel families feed the same inner tiled routine. It handles partial M tiles but counts only full K and N tiles. The separate `exl3_gemm_shape_compat` helper checks both divisibilities; the native dispatchers do not call it.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": ["call_3393a7ae877d4e478e1107ca61ddc70b", "call_0ac71f39100d4148895fe03424ec3c17", "call_8e5e7f134dba4f0fb8059a9f3615bcc4", "call_6ee8c689f6b64f2d9479e75c6cf67a79"]
        },
        {
          "text": "OLD/Ampere now require N divisible by 256 before entering either the at-most-four-bit branch or the N<4096 branch that can choose shape 3 at K>8192. Ada adds the same gate to its at-most-three-bit branch. An N divisible by 128 but not 256 also fails the 512-column test, so it falls through to shape 2 on those tiers.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": ["call_40831d8b34cf4edeb9683ccbde66ab82", "call_0ac71f39100d4148895fe03424ec3c17", "call_3393a7ae877d4e478e1107ca61ddc70b"]
        },
        {
          "text": "Hopper/Blackwell add the same gate to the seven-or-more-bit branch for N≤8192, where shape 3 requires K>32768. For lower bitrates and N≤4096, the repaired, gated rule picks shape 3 only when K>8192 and bits≥3. The earlier single-GEMM exception still takes priority: two- or four-bit weights with K≤2048 use shape 1, which also has a 128-column tile. Shape 4's existing 512-column gates are unchanged; the OLD/Ampere test also requires K×N>4096² (16,777,216 weight positions) and at most six bits.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": ["call_40831d8b34cf4edeb9683ccbde66ab82", "call_0ac71f39100d4148895fe03424ec3c17", "call_3393a7ae877d4e478e1107ca61ddc70b"]
        },
        {
          "text": "The scalar transcription checked 196,608 combinations of three tier groups, eight K values, widths in steps of 128, all eight bitrates, and both `multi` settings. N was incompatible with the selected tile in 20,208 parent cases and none of the patched cases in this sample. At Ampere, K=4096, N=2176, and four bits, the model changes from shape 3 covering 2,048 columns to shape 2 covering all 2,176. At Hopper/Blackwell, K=16384, N=4096, and three bits, it changes from shape 2 to shape 3; both cover all columns.",
          "basis": "execution",
          "evidence": ["call_2d7e3e5b3dc440928ef05d2ecf8c7573"]
        },
        {
          "text": "After selection, the existing dispatch uses the shape index for block size and tile-based launch limits, then combines it with the codebook slot to select a function pointer from the bitrate- and output-precision-specific table. The patch changes which specialization is chosen, not the packed-weight format, kernel implementation, or precision. The added `DBGI3` line is commented out.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": ["call_40831d8b34cf4edeb9683ccbde66ab82", "call_0ac71f39100d4148895fe03424ec3c17", "call_3393a7ae877d4e478e1107ca61ddc70b"]
        }
      ]
